    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our premier asset, carrying an elite 81.88 efficiency score. While his base projection is strong, the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and the exploitability of the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery\u2014which boosts his stolen base upside against a high-efficiency catcher\u2014makes him our clear focal point. **Jackson Merrill** also provides significant value (75.27), leveraging a juicy matchup against an opposing arm with a 5.59 xERA, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains a highly efficient play (73.66) due to substantial platoon advantages and a favorable SP matchup that drives his output well above his baseline expectations.\n\nOur lineup construction emphasizes capitalizing on these soft pitching matchups, though we remain cautious with our catcher rotation. **Liam Hicks** (57.76) edges out **Drake Baldwin** (53.96) for the primary spot today, largely because **Drake Baldwin** faces a tougher pitching profile with a documented historical BvP struggle that suppresses his ceiling. We are currently navigating a depleted bench; with **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg** all unavailable due to IL status or rest, we lack high-leverage pinch-hitting alternatives, forcing us to rely heavily on the primary starters. We are monitoring the status of players like **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Nasim Nunez** to ensure we don't bleed game caps, as the limited depth behind **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Franklin Arias**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Tommy White** necessitates strict adherence to our efficiency thresholds to protect our season-long category standings.",
